    "linkedin:010dc19bd3544a62521041fc": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Software Engineer, Full Stack (AI) (Customer-Facing)",
        "company": "StoneApp by Stone Grid",
        "location": "USA",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4494037841",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "2026-11-23T00:00:00+00:00",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "About the Company\nStone Grid builds StoneApp, the ERP platform that 100+ stone and countertop fabricators across North America use to run their entire business, from quoting and CAD to production, scheduling and installation. Stone fabrication is a large, hands-on industry that still runs largely on paper, spreadsheets and disconnected systems. We're on a mission to revolutionize it: using AI and automation to transform how fabricators quote, plan, cut and install, and building the modern platform the industry runs on. Customers also bring us in as experts: we consult on their operational problems and build software solutions for them. We're a small, remote-first team that ships like a much bigger one, because every engineer builds with AI coding agents.\nAbout the Role\nThis is an engineering role first: most of your time goes to building and shipping StoneApp features. You'll also work directly with fabricators, on calls and on-site, as a trusted technical advisor. You'll learn how their shops run, diagnose their problems, and shape the features and paid solutions that fix them.\nLocation and travel: Fully remote within the US, with travel to customer sites a couple of times a quarter.\nResponsibilities\nBuild and ship features across React/TypeScript and .NET, using AI coding agents\nConsult with customers: understand their operations, recommend solutions and help scope paid projects\nVisit shops occasionally to learn the industry firsthand and help with rollouts\nTurn what you learn into clear requirements, then build the solution\nOwn production issues with customers through to resolution\nQualifications\nNew grads and early-career engineers welcome\nWe care more about what you've built than years of experience\nUS-based and authorized to work in the US. We're unable to sponsor work visas at this time\nRequired Skills\nStrong engineering fundamentals: you break down messy problems and ship working software\nExcellent spoken and written English, and confidence advising customers directly\nA fast learner who gets comfortable in a new industry quickly\nAbility or interest in building with AI coding agents (we'll train you)\nWilling to travel a couple of times a quarter\nPreferred Skills\nConsulting, implementation or solutions engineering experience\nERP, manufacturing or construction software\nReact/TypeScript, .NET or SQL\nPay range and compensation package\nWhat we offer: remote-first work with occasional travel, real ownership of products and consulting projects fabricators rely on daily, hands-on AI and automation work, and room to grow\nCompensation: $60,000–$120,000 base, depending on experience. New grads typically start toward the lower end of the range\nBenefits: paid time off and reimbursement for work-related expenses (travel, AI coding tools and more)\nHiring process: a short application question, a take-home project (2–3 hours), one interview, and a paid 1–2 week trial project\nEqual Opportunity Statement\nStone Grid is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applicants of all backgrounds and do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.",
