    "linkedin:06ac88dd40fe2e0a1b8faa62": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Early Career C#/.NET Developer (Healthcare Applications)",
        "company": "Gainwell Technologies",
        "location": "Arizona, USA",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484616299",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "2026-11-23T00:00:00+00:00",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "Be part of a team that unleashes the power of leading-edge technologies to help improve the health and well-being of those most vulnerable in our country and communities. Working at Gainwell carries its rewards. You’ll have an incredible opportunity to grow your career in a company that values work flexibility, learning, and career development. You’ll add to your technical credentials and certifications while enjoying a generous, flexible vacation policy and educational assistance. We also have comprehensive leadership and technical development academies to help build your skills and capabilities.\nSummary\nAs an Early Career C#/.NET Developer (Healthcare Applications) at Gainwell, you can contribute your skills as we harness the power of technology to help our clients improve the health and well-being of the members they serve — a community’s most vulnerable. Connect your passion with purpose, teaming with people who thrive on finding innovative solutions to some of healthcare’s biggest challenges. Here are the details on this position.\nThe SUR Developer I is an entry-level software development role responsible for supporting the design, development, testing, maintenance, and enhancement of applications supporting the Surveillance and Utilization Review (SUR) program. Under the guidance of senior developers and technical leads, this position contributes to application development, defect resolution, system enhancements, and production support activities.\nYour role in our mission\nDevelop, test, and maintain application components using Oracle PL/SQL, C#, and ASP.NET.\nAssist in the analysis of business and technical requirements.\nCreate and modify database objects including packages, procedures, functions, and queries.\nSupport application troubleshooting, defect remediation, and root cause analysis.\nParticipate in code reviews and follow established coding standards and SDLC processes.\nCollaborate with business analysts, testers, and senior developers to deliver system enhancements.\nDocument technical designs, code changes, and operational procedures.\nSupport production issues and participate in on-call activities as assigned.\nContribute to continuous improvement initiatives and application modernization efforts.\nWhat We're Looking For\n0 to 2 years of experience in software development, application support, or a related technical role, with a Bachelor's degree in Information Systems, Software Engineering, Computer Science, or equivalent experience.\nBasic programming and database experience with Oracle Database, PL/SQL, C#, ASP.NET, SQL, and relational database concepts.\nUnderstanding of the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC), software development best practices, web application development, and troubleshooting methodologies.\nStrong analytical, problem solving, communication, and collaboration skills, with the ability to work effectively in a team environment and support business objectives.\nPreferred experience or exposure to SSRS, Entity Framework, Azure DevOps/Git, Visual Studio, and healthcare, Medicaid, or government systems.\nWhat You Should Expect In This Role\nFully remote opportunity with the option to work anywhere within the United States\nOpportunities to travel through your work (0-10%)\nWillingness to work a flexible schedule to accommodate business needs and travel as required\nVideo cameras must be used during all interviews, as well as during the initial week of orientation\nThe deadline to submit applications for this posting is December 30, 2026\nThe pay range for this position is $46,600.00 - $66,600.00 per year, however, the base pay offered may vary depending on geographic region, internal equity, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience among other factors. Put your passion to work at Gainwell. You’ll have the opportunity to grow your career in a company that values work flexibility, learning, and career development. All salaried, full-time candidates are eligible for our generous, flexible vacation policy, a 401(k) employer match, comprehensive health benefits, and educational assistance. We also have a variety of leadership and technical development academies to help build your skills and capabilities.\nWe believe nothing is impossible when you bring together people who care deeply about making healthcare work better for everyone. Build your career with Gainwell, an industry leader. You’ll be joining a company where collaboration, innovation, and inclusion fuel our growth. Learn more about Gainwell at our company website and visit our Careers site for all available job role openings.\nGainwell Technologies is an Equal Opportunity Employer, where all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical condition), age, sexual orientation, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. Gainwell Technologies defines “wages” and “wage rates” to include “all forms of pay, including, but not limited to, salary, overtime pay, bonuses, stock, stock options, profit sharing and bonus plans, life insurance, vacation and holiday pay, cleaning or gasoline allowances, hotel accommodations, reimbursement for travel expenses, and benefits.",
